# AWS Config Test

This is a simple test to show how you can use the `aws` secret with a Helm chart.

## How does it work?

It's a very basic example that shows how you can get your AWS credentials from an SSM paramater and then use them in a Kubernetes secret. 

The chart uses the [vault-secrets-provider](https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami/vault-secrets) Bitnami chart as a way of getting the values into Vault.

Then it uses the [helm-vault-plugin](https://github.com/helm-vault-plugin/) Helm plugin to fetch the vault values into a Kubernetes secret.

And finally, we use the [bitnami/aws-config-secret](https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami/aws-config-secret) Bitnami chart to get the AWS configuration from the secrets.

## The Chart

The chart has only one dependency which is the `vault-secrets` chart mentioned above.

When the chart is installed, the following files are created:

```
├── charts/
│   └── vault-secrets
│       ├── README.md
│       ├── charts/
│       │   ├── bitnami-helm-chart-example/
│       │   │   ...
│       │   ├── vault/
│       │   │   ...
│       │   └── templates/
│       │       ├── configmap.yaml
│       │       ├── livenessprobe.yaml
│       │       ├── readinessprobe.yaml
│       │       └── serviceaccount.yaml
│       ├── charts.yaml
│       ├── images.yaml
│       ├── params.yaml
│       └── requirements.yaml
└── Chart.yaml
```

### Changes made to the `Chart.yaml`

We changed the version of the `chart` to be `1.0.0`. This will ensure that the chart is deployed when we run `helm install ...`.

### Changes made to the `values.yaml`

We set the following parameters:

* `secretName`: this is the name of the secret that will be created by the chart.
* `secrets`: this is the list of secrets that we want to create in Vault and their values.

In our case, we have two secrets: `accessKeyID`, and `secretAccessKey`. We also specify the path where these keys should be stored in Vault. In this case, they are under the `AWS` namespace and the `config` key.

### Chart Dependencies

The chart depends on the `vault-secrets` chart which is uploaded to Bitnami Charts Repository using the following command:

```bash
helm repo add bitnami https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami
helm dep update apps.vault-secrets
```

You can see more about how to upload charts to the repository here: https://docs.helm.sh/docs/topics/charts/#uploading-charts-to-the-repository

## Usage

To deploy the chart, make sure you have the [Helm CLI](https://helm.sh/docs/intro/install/) installed and run the following command:

```bash
helm upgrade --install aws-config-test ./charts/aws-config-test
```

This will install the chart and create the following resources:

* Secret: `aws-config-test-access-key-id`
* Secret: `aws-config-test-secret-access-key`
* Secret: `aws-config-test-role-session-token`
